# USB-only block device policy (Phase 2)
#
# This policy is expressed for both popular device managers; whichever binary
# is present in the initramfs can ingest the relevant stanza.
#
# udev (if available) should drop or ignore any block device whose ENV{ID_BUS}
# is not usb before it becomes visible in /dev.  When udev is missing, the
# same enforcement logic is handled by `ouroboros/scripts/assert_usb_only_environment.sh`.
#
# Example udev rule:
# ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_BUS}!="usb", GOTO="ouroboros_usb_only_end"
# ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_BUS}=="usb", TAG+="ouroboros_usb_only"
# LABEL="ouroboros_usb_only_end"
#
# BusyBox mdev (if available) can also invoke the assertion helper to detect
# non-USB block nodes as they appear:
# pattern      mode   uid   gid   command
# *            0600   root  root  /ouroboros/scripts/assert_usb_only_environment.sh --mdev-hook
#
# Once a proper device manager is wired in (Phase 7), this rule file can be
# migrated verbatim under /etc/udev/rules.d/ (or /etc/mdev.conf) to enforce
# the USB-only surface declaratively.
